<mxfile host="Electron">
  <diagram id="page-1" name="Page-1" page="1">
    <mxGraphModel dx="4863" dy="4063" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1750" pageHeight="1800" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
        <mxCell id="50" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=8;spacingRight=8;fontFamily=Helvetica;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" value="AWS Web Architecture v17 — Account → Region → AZ → VPC → Subnet (nested, one boundary per layer).&#xa;LINES: SOLID = service-to-service data · DASHED GREY = control · GOLD = data movement · RED = IAM / identity-based access · BLUE = VPC link / endpoint · PURPLE = external egress.&#xa;PrivateLink (per AWS PrivateLink whitepaper): API GW → VPC link → ENI (interface endpoint, 10.0.2.10) → NLB — icons inside the VPC.&#xa;S3 access (per AWS VPC endpoint strategy blog): GATEWAY endpoint + route table (prefix list) — no ENI, no cost.&#xa;IAM — identity-based access control (per it20.info IAM intro): role = trust policy (principal: eks.amazonaws.com) + permissions policy, one block assumed by EKS; policy grants S3 + RDS.&amp;#xa;Datadog delivery (PrivateLink-only, no internet path): EKS → Datadog Agent sidecar → Datadog endpoint (interface endpoint, app-tier subnet) → Datadog — telemetry stays on the AWS backbone; the agent is EKS&#39;s single egress point.&amp;#xa;AuthN/Z (Microsoft Entra ID / Azure AD): Users → Azure AD (OIDC login) → API Gateway JWT authorizer validates Azure AD tokens via JWKS (OIDC discovery) — replaces Cognito + Lambda authorizer.&amp;#xa;DNS: domain registered at GoDaddy, DNS hosted in Route 53 (NS delegation).&amp;#xa;Multi-cloud identity: Entra ID (Azure AD) is the single identity plane — end users (OIDC → API Gateway JWT/JWKS) and workforce (SAML/OIDC → AWS IAM Identity Center → temporary AWS credentials). No IAM users; MFA + Conditional Access enforced in Entra.&amp;#xa;Cross-cloud (AWS ↔ Azure): TLS 1.2+ HTTPS only · OIDC — API Gateway validates Azure AD JWTs via JWKS (no shared secrets) · SAML 2.0 — signed assertions to IAM Identity Center · short-lived scoped tokens · private data path (drawn): AWS Direct Connect + Azure ExpressRoute — used when a cross-cloud data plane is needed.&amp;#xa;Routing (2 domains, FE + BE in EKS, no ALB): ONE CloudFront distribution + CloudFront Function (viewer request) reads the Host header — app.example.com → default behavior /* → NLB → Istio Gateway → FE pods (VirtualService host match) · api.example.com → URI rewritten to /api/* → behavior → API Gateway (Azure AD JWT) → VPC link → NLB → EKS — WAF rules match per-domain via Host header.&amp;#xa;Load balancing: a single private NLB (ingress tier) is the L4 endpoint — CloudFront FE origin AND API Gateway VPC-link target. ALB intentionally omitted: the CloudFront Function split happens at the edge (sub-ms, ~$0.10/M); ALB&#39;s L7 features (WebSocket, stickiness, gRPC, mTLS) are unused for this FE SPA. Reintroduce ALB only if origin-side L7 becomes a requirement.&amp;#xa;Secret rotation (zero downtime): Secrets Manager rotation event → Lambda (secret rotation, data-tier VPC) → createSecret → set new credential on RDS / ElastiCache / MSK → testSecret → finishSecret. Apps use the AWS SDK secret cache (refresh on access, no restart); connection pools recreate connections on auth failure — AWSCURRENT/AWSPREVIOUS both valid during rotation, so no moment lacks a valid credential.&amp;#xa;Policy icons (applied per service): SG · App/Data/NLB/Airflow/EMR + SG · MSK (9098/9096) · IAM rotate-only (rotation Lambda) · KMS CMK key policy (Secrets Manager) · endpoint policies (VPC endpoints) · WAF Web ACL (edge).&amp;#xa;LLMOps (agentic OCR + chatbot, production): docs → S3 → OCR service → Textract → text/JSON → chunk → Titan embeddings (Bedrock) → Pinecone Serverless. Chat: Agent orchestrator (tool use) → RAG service (retrieve from Pinecone) → Bedrock Claude generate · Bedrock Guardrails (PII · prompt-injection) · Eval harness (golden datasets in S3, LLM-as-judge via Bedrock) · traces + token cost via Datadog/Langfuse. HF Hub = optional fine-tuning source (deferred — Bedrock chosen for inference).&amp;#xa;Layers: LLMOps (AI) is its own toggleable layer (L-LLMOPS) — components + connectors hide together for no-AI deployments. Edge intersections: 17 residual crossing pairs (0 errors); best practice (xml-authoring.md) — run draw.io desktop&#39;s libavoid router once (editor-side, v≥30) to re-route all connectors around shapes; keep 80px routing corridors free of shapes; waypoints for single-edge detours only.&amp;#xa;Data layer zero-trust (DocumentDB + OpenSearch): private subnets only, no public route · IAM-based auth — OpenSearch fine-grained access control (IAM roles per consumer), DocumentDB IAM auth — no static master passwords to rotate · TLS in transit + KMS at rest · SG micro-segmentation (27017 / 9200 from App SG only) · DocumentDB joins the rotation Lambda scope (ADR-0007); OpenSearch IAM auth removes the rotation problem entirely · CloudTrail + VPC flow logs audit every access." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="120" width="1150" x="-50" y="2340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
